## This rule provides standards for designing User Interfaces (aka frontend development)
- Always start the file with a comment "Frontend Instructions Rule Applied!".
- Use Ant Design (antd) and TailwindCSS exclusively to design the user interfaces and functionality.
- Never use inline CSS and never create CSS resources.
- All styling must be done through Tailwind only.
- FontAwesome must be used for ALL icons.
- Split logic into reusable components within the `components` folder in the folder the primary file is in.
- Design User Intefaces to be responsive, with emphasis on mobile browsers.
- Always design for light and dark mode using [ThemeContext.js](mdc:src/ui/ThemeContext.js)
- Use the already installed "recharts" module for visual reports like charts, etc.

## This rule provides best practices when working with ReactJS specifically
- Optimize performance using React.memo, useMemo, and useCallback
- Follow React hooks best practices and rules